WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.100
In cystic fibrosis, the
airway problem begins with abnormal

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.884
epithelial ion transport.

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:09.380
The supplied chapter describes
defective chloride transport and exaggerated

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:12.953
sodium absorption, which
deplete airway surface liquid.

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:16.340
Watch the mucus layer lose water and become harder

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:16.835
to move.

00:00:17.166 --> 00:00:21.040
Cilia cannot clear the
adherent secretions effectively, and bacteria

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:22.197
remain in the airway.

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:24.823
Inflammation then amplifies the problem.

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:29.490
Degraded neutrophils release DNA
and filamentous actin, adding to

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:30.489
mucus viscosity.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:35.380
Thick secretions obstruct small
airways, while chronic inflammation can

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:37.523
lead to bronchiectasis and fibrosis.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:40.900
The drawing shows a
mechanism, not a scaled measurement

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:43.580
of mucus thickness or a prediction for an individual

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:44.136
child.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:48.235
Distinguish this process from
newborn respiratory distress syndrome.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:52.395
In that disorder, inadequate
surfactant in the immature lung

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:53.848
promotes alveolar collapse.

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:58.067
Both can impair breathing,
but the initiating defect and

00:00:58.160 --> 00:00:59.964
the affected surface are different.
